{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1752 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "779480473c7fca043a97580650f3b03780925d844cc66e820e732905218ca3ee" :edb/db-before-t 1751 :edb/db-after-t 1752 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535064 50 #inst "2026-10-08T16:02:22.098Z" 13194139535064 true] [17592186147392 1020 #edb/ref 17592186329261 13194139535064 true] [17592186147392 1020 #edb/ref 17592186329268 13194139535064 true] [17592186147393 1020 #edb/ref 17592186329275 13194139535064 true] [17592186147393 1020 #edb/ref 17592186329282 13194139535064 true] [17592186147393 1020 #edb/ref 17592186329289 13194139535064 true] [17592186329261 1017 #edb/ref 17592186329262 13194139535064 true] [17592186329261 1089 "q-109021" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329261 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535064 true] [17592186329261 1100 "The substitution $z={y}^{m}$ for some real number $m$ transforms the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\frac{y}{x}={x}^{3}{y}^{3/4}\n$$\n\ninto an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)+P(x)z(x)=Q(x).$ What is the function $Q(x)?$" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329261 1113 #uuid "3bbe7f28-efd3-56e9-a3e7-84fe99064a40" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329261 1145 "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=\\frac{1}{x},\\,q(x)={x}^{3},\\,n=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{3/4},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-3/4}\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\frac{{y}^{1/4}}{x}={x}^{3}.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{1/4}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{-3/4}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-3/4}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, equation $(∗)$ can be written as a linear equation in $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n4\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}\\,z={x}^{3}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the above equation in standard form, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{4x}\\,z=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Q(x)=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{4}.$" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329262 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329263 13194139535064 true] [17592186329262 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329264 13194139535064 true] [17592186329262 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329265 13194139535064 true] [17592186329262 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329266 13194139535064 true] [17592186329262 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329267 13194139535064 true] [17592186329262 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535064 true] [17592186329262 1041 "selection" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329262 1104 #edb/ref 17592186329265 13194139535064 true] [17592186329262 1110 #uuid "acb9739b-df49-5f18-bb5b-0417ac37adcd" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329263 1034 "-4{x}^{3}" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329263 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535064 true] [17592186329263 1111 #uuid "e2428fd3-c0b5-51a3-8140-ab5648378d54" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329264 1034 "\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{3}" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329264 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535064 true] [17592186329264 1111 #uuid "61090dbc-9ec4-5a3c-8b6c-8decc70cf6a4" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329265 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{4}" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329265 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535064 true] [17592186329265 1111 #uuid "6a259432-1b1e-5ebb-b9ae-c48fa783330e" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329266 1034 "\\frac{1}{4x}" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329266 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535064 true] [17592186329266 1111 #uuid "32af292a-783e-5ab6-8c9b-03fbd575cebb" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329267 1034 "-\\frac{1}{3x}" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329267 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535064 true] [17592186329267 1111 #uuid "88fb7b17-1892-534e-983a-5947c47d555a" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329268 1017 #edb/ref 17592186329269 13194139535064 true] [17592186329268 1089 "q-109024" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329268 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535064 true] [17592186329268 1100 "The substitution $z={y}^{m}$ for some real number $m$ transforms the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}-xy=\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{y}}{{x}^{5}}\n$$\n\ninto an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)+P(x)z(x)=Q(x).$ What is the function $P(x)?$" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329268 1113 #uuid "023ae6da-320c-5d9f-893c-3cafd754c018" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329268 1145 "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=-x,\\,q(x)={x}^{-5},\\,n=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{1/3},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-1/3}\\frac{dy}{dx}-x{y}^{2/3}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{2/3}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{-1/3}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-1/3}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, equation $(∗)$ can be written as a linear equation in $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-x\\,z=\\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the above equation in standard form, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{2x}{3}\\,z=\\frac{2}{3{x}^{5}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=-\\frac{2x}{3}.$" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329269 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329270 13194139535064 true] [17592186329269 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329271 13194139535064 true] [17592186329269 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329272 13194139535064 true] [17592186329269 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329273 13194139535064 true] [17592186329269 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329274 13194139535064 true] [17592186329269 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535064 true] [17592186329269 1041 "selection" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329269 1104 #edb/ref 17592186329272 13194139535064 true] [17592186329269 1110 #uuid "6b3de7a7-0d97-5379-80f9-4e237ee41ece" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329270 1034 "\\frac{2}{3{x}^{5}}" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329270 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535064 true] [17592186329270 1111 #uuid "11354af7-b2c7-520f-95c1-717104e7bedf" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329271 1034 "\\frac{3}{x}" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329271 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535064 true] [17592186329271 1111 #uuid "31df7db3-f90e-57fa-9036-59679e679851" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329272 1034 "-\\frac{2x}{3}" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329272 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535064 true] [17592186329272 1111 #uuid "0623ed2a-bdd6-5cae-b2c5-e807cdf30235" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329273 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{5}}{3}" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329273 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535064 true] [17592186329273 1111 #uuid "0bd19702-9c54-5140-ba6b-1087862af8ef" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329274 1034 "-\\frac{3x}{2}" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329274 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535064 true] [17592186329274 1111 #uuid "8638cc8e-5c91-5ab9-ba33-82dd1153cc34" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329275 1017 #edb/ref 17592186329276 13194139535064 true] [17592186329275 1089 "q-109027" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329275 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535064 true] [17592186329275 1100 "Find the general solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3{x}^{2}y={x}^{2}{y}^{-4}.\n$$" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329275 1113 #uuid "90997a63-8b0a-5ca6-9670-b13bb0d8de17" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329275 1145 "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=-3{x}^{2},\\,q(x)={x}^{2},\\,n=-4.\n$$\n\nFirst, we multiply the differential equation by ${y}^{4},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{4}\\frac{dy}{dx}-3{x}^{2}{y}^{5}={x}^{2}.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{5}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=5{y}^{4}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{4}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-3{x}^{2}z={x}^{2}\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is linear, so we can use the method of integrating factors. But first, we write the above equation in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-15{x}^{2}z=5{x}^{2}\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=-15{x}^{2},\\,Q(x)=5{x}^{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (-15{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-5{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)={e}^{-5{x}^{3}}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-5{x}^{3}}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-15{x}^{2}z) & ={e}^{-5{x}^{3}}\\cdot (5{x}^{2}) \\\\ {e}^{-5{x}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-15{x}^{2}z{e}^{-5{x}^{3}} & =5{x}^{2}{e}^{-5{x}^{3}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{e}^{-5{x}^{3}}) & =5{x}^{2}{e}^{-5{x}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{e}^{-5{x}^{3}})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 5{x}^{2}{e}^{-5{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ z{e}^{-5{x}^{3}} & =-\\frac{{e}^{-5{x}^{3}}}{3}+{C}_{1} \\\\ z & =\\frac{C{e}^{5{x}^{3}}-1}{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=3{C}_{1}.$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{5}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{5}=\\frac{C{e}^{5{x}^{3}}-1}{3}\\,⇒\\,y=\\sqrt[5]{\\frac{C{e}^{5{x}^{3}}-1}{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329276 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329277 13194139535064 true] [17592186329276 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329278 13194139535064 true] [17592186329276 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329279 13194139535064 true] [17592186329276 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329280 13194139535064 true] [17592186329276 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329281 13194139535064 true] [17592186329276 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535064 true] [17592186329276 1041 "selection" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329276 1104 #edb/ref 17592186329281 13194139535064 true] [17592186329276 1110 #uuid "69e4b3a8-2ec3-5c49-a6cd-2f7311b25459" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329277 1034 "y=\\sqrt[5]{\\frac{C-{e}^{5{x}^{3}}}{{x}^{2}}}" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329277 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535064 true] [17592186329277 1111 #uuid "e26eb2a3-f820-5d12-b6dd-71854a0f9967" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329278 1034 "y=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{C{e}^{3{x}^{2}}-1}{2}}" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329278 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535064 true] [17592186329278 1111 #uuid "2b08c91a-aca9-5016-8503-b32cc4bb1e66" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329279 1034 "y=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{C-{e}^{3{x}^{2}}}{x}}" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329279 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535064 true] [17592186329279 1111 #uuid "6b5c237e-1202-5915-8012-04fdd3a5e0e7" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329280 1034 "y=\\sqrt[5]{\\frac{C{e}^{x}-1}{3}}" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329280 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535064 true] [17592186329280 1111 #uuid "cb18262f-5203-5e13-acf6-8c9af8fb1ef5" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329281 1034 "y=\\sqrt[5]{\\frac{C{e}^{5{x}^{3}}-1}{3}}" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329281 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535064 true] [17592186329281 1111 #uuid "b4d54925-04a5-52ae-8425-88472a7940b7" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329282 1017 #edb/ref 17592186329283 13194139535064 true] [17592186329282 1089 "q-109028" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329282 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535064 true] [17592186329282 1100 "Find the general solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y=-x{y}^{3}.\n$$" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329282 1113 #uuid "21b39c4d-cfb3-59e7-bfe5-8b7a15dc1142" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329282 1145 "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=1,\\,q(x)=-x,\\,n=3.\n$$\n\nFirst, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{3},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-3}\\frac{dy}{dx}+{y}^{-2}=-x.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{-2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=-2{y}^{-3}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-3}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+z=-x\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is linear, so we can use the method of integrating factors. But first, we write the above equation in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-2z=2x\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=-2,\\,Q(x)=2x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (-2)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)={e}^{-2x}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-2x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-2z) & ={e}^{-2x}\\cdot (2x) \\\\ {e}^{-2x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-2z{e}^{-2x} & =2x{e}^{-2x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{e}^{-2x}) & =2x{e}^{-2x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{e}^{-2x})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x{e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ z{e}^{-2x} & =-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2x}(2x+1)+{C}_{1} \\\\ z & =\\frac{C{e}^{2x}-2x-1}{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=2{C}_{1}.$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{-2}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{-2}=\\frac{C{e}^{2x}-2x-1}{2}\\,⇒\\,y=\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{C{e}^{2x}-2x-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329283 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329284 13194139535064 true] [17592186329283 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329285 13194139535064 true] [17592186329283 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329286 13194139535064 true] [17592186329283 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329287 13194139535064 true] [17592186329283 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329288 13194139535064 true] [17592186329283 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535064 true] [17592186329283 1041 "selection" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329283 1104 #edb/ref 17592186329284 13194139535064 true] [17592186329283 1110 #uuid "581e3af7-db14-5b36-b226-a78708939c61" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329284 1034 "y=\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{C{e}^{2x}-2x-1}}" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329284 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535064 true] [17592186329284 1111 #uuid "08c1b73a-ddb0-5185-a9d2-4295e6b3ab74" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329285 1034 "y=\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{C{e}^{x}-1}}" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329285 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535064 true] [17592186329285 1111 #uuid "b312561b-17a7-5f1b-9e25-632d8ccc99c0" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329286 1034 "y=\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{2x}{C+{e}^{2x}}}" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329286 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535064 true] [17592186329286 1111 #uuid "55e0d93a-8572-52e1-a086-959899b473e3" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329287 1034 "y=\\frac{2x+1}{C-{e}^{2x}}" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329287 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535064 true] [17592186329287 1111 #uuid "c26b94f6-7d3f-5f6e-a2cd-3fe2d88b4bf4" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329288 1034 "y=\\frac{2}{C{e}^{x}-2x}" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329288 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535064 true] [17592186329288 1111 #uuid "ced8eb65-de8c-580d-9481-5a07bfd6fd04" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329289 1017 #edb/ref 17592186329290 13194139535064 true] [17592186329289 1089 "q-109154" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329289 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535064 true] [17592186329289 1100 "Find the general solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{y}{x}=\\sqrt{x}\\,{y}^{2}.\n$$" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329289 1113 #uuid "692fec97-1d1e-5270-a23f-3b8552e51e1f" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329289 1145 "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=-\\frac{1}{x},\\,q(x)=\\sqrt{x},\\,n=2.\n$$\n\nFirst, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{2},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-2}\\frac{dy}{dx}-\\frac{1}{x}{y}^{-1}=\\sqrt{x}.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=-{y}^{-2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n-\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{1}{x}z=\\sqrt{x}\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is linear, so we can use the method of integrating factors. But first, we write the above equation in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}z=-\\sqrt{x}\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=\\frac{1}{x},\\,Q(x)=-\\sqrt{x}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (1/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)=x$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}z) & =x\\cdot (-\\sqrt{x}) \\\\ x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+z & =-x\\sqrt{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(xz) & =-{x}^{3/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(xz)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int -{x}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ xz & =-\\frac{2{x}^{5/2}}{5}+{C}_{1} \\\\ z & =\\frac{C-2{x}^{5/2}}{5x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=5{C}_{1}.$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{-1}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{-1}=\\frac{C-2{x}^{5/2}}{5x}\\,⇒\\,y=\\frac{5x}{C-2{x}^{5/2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329290 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329291 13194139535064 true] [17592186329290 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329292 13194139535064 true] [17592186329290 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329293 13194139535064 true] [17592186329290 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329294 13194139535064 true] [17592186329290 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329295 13194139535064 true] [17592186329290 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535064 true] [17592186329290 1041 "selection" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329290 1104 #edb/ref 17592186329293 13194139535064 true] [17592186329290 1110 #uuid "1f367fc4-b717-5b6e-81f2-788d821286e9" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329291 1034 "y=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{C-5{x}^{5/2}}" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329291 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535064 true] [17592186329291 1111 #uuid "04841c1a-60c3-57db-91b5-dcbeab6a0fef" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329292 1034 "y=\\frac{5x}{C+{x}^{3/2}}" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329292 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535064 true] [17592186329292 1111 #uuid "9f7699e8-a6fa-5ae7-bd4a-9cb54c850ce0" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329293 1034 "y=\\frac{5x}{C-2{x}^{5/2}}" 13194139535064 true] [17592186329293 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 1319413953